>> title: Japanese Milk Bread
>> category: Breads
>> tags: bread, japanese, milk, tangzhong, sandwich
>> counters: Bakery
>> aka: shokupan, 食パン, milk bread, Hokkaido milk bread, pain de mie
>> servings: 12
>> time: 4 hr
>> slack: narrow — the tangzhong goes in cooled, because warm paste kills the rise and lumps bake through the loaf as streaks

>> step: cook to a paste, cool
Cook @bread flour{3%Tbs}(25 g) with @whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL) over low heat until thick, then cool.

>> step: stir into the tangzhong
Stir @warm whole milk{1/2%cup}(120 mL), @granulated sugar{1/4%cup}(50 g), @instant yeast{2 1/4%tsp}(7 g), and @egg{1%large} into @&(~1)tangzhong{}.

>> step: add and knead 8 min
Add @bread flour{2 1/2%cup}(340 g), @nonfat dry milk{2%Tbs}(14 g), and @table salt{1 1/2%tsp}(9 g) to @&(~1)mixture{}, then knead ~{8%min}.

>> step: knead in, rise until doubled
Knead @softened unsalted butter{4%Tbs}(55 g) into @&(~1)dough{}, then rise until doubled, ~{1%hour}.

>> step: roll three coils, proof in a 9x5-in loaf pan
Roll @&(~1)dough{} into three coils and proof in a #9x5-in loaf pan{} for ~{1%hour}.

>> step: bake 350°F 35 min
Bake @&(~1)loaf{} at 350°F for ~{35%min}.
